From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:41:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS shell: return to library on quit with full host and GPU
 teardown

When a game runs inside the Route C multi-game iOS shell (DmShell), quitting from the in-game quit prompt or Home-button hold previously terminated the process because the host, GPU backend, guest address space, and framework static state were initialized once per process.

Add dm_host_teardown_for_shell() and dm_shell_return_to_library() so quitting a game inside DmShell tears down the active session and returns the window to the library without exiting the app:
- Park and join guest and host helper threads (dm_threads_park_all, dm_host_threads_join_all), waking blocked waits across guest clock, OE, GFX, audio, network, and web applets, and suspending lingering threads only when their PC is inside guest module code so host locks are never held by a suspended thread.
- Drain and release Metal/NVN/VK/GL queues, command buffers, textures, shader/pipeline caches, and presentation threads, and stop/dispose all audio units (including handing in-flight AU_CANCELED starts to au_start_device for disposal).
- Guard front_ios.m focus/quit callbacks with g_quitting during async teardown so scene transitions cannot race with teardown.
- Unmap the 5 GiB guest address space and backing swap file in dm_svc_teardown(), and snapshot/restore the game framework's writable data segments (__data, __common, __bss via mincore(MINCORE_INCORE | MINCORE_PAGED_OUT) + MAP_FIXED zero-page re-mapping) while preserving process-lifetime keys/locks in __DATA,__dm_keep.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Return to the DmShell game library on quit instead of terminating the process, tearing down guest threads, audio, Metal/GPU resources, the 5 GiB guest address space, and restoring framework data segments.
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#809
